{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-65117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+16y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-65117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-4,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4A\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-4B\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4=4A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-65117" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a367bed387ad3efa01cc9a4b30aaf85108e7d6b45385a89adeeec85b0adc149"} {"question" "q-65117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-65117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-65117" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}+Bx{e}^{-x},\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0,\\,y(0)=8,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=8$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=8.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-x}-Bx{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+B=0.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=8$ gives $B=8.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a367bed387ad3efa01cc9a4b30aaf85108e7d6b45385a89adeeec85b0adc149"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=8{e}^{-x}+4x{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{-x}+6x{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{-x}-4x{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "y=8{e}^{-x}-8x{e}^{-x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+17y=0,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-11.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $P$ and $Q$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nP=-1.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-11,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+{e}^{-x}(-4P\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+4Q\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x).\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-11$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+4Q=-11.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=-1$ gives $Q=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a367bed387ad3efa01cc9a4b30aaf85108e7d6b45385a89adeeec85b0adc149"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"] ["math" "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-94031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-130353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-130353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-9,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x-9B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9=9A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-130353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a367bed387ad3efa01cc9a4b30aaf85108e7d6b45385a89adeeec85b0adc149"} {"question" "q-130353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085efb3ba3740bb7be6767e0c172f15fc55d"} {"question" "q-130353" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x"] ["math" "y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x"] ["math" "y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14074931/state.json" "file_sha256" "6e6523f8b9d07bef98c9af0be412085ef